From 2050733bc6571383fe954bea422f8da0f8cdd67d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 03:27:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): blocked notices show the card's exact human ask,
 not clipped event prose [daveey]

A blocked chat showed only an opaque, 160-char-clipped event reason ("...
identity boundary ... Initiate HANDOFF ...") and a task id; the validated
human_request (action/why/scope) never reached the notice.

Five whys:
1. Notice was opaque: local (tui session_notifications), remote
   (kanban_remote_notices) and gateway (kanban_watchers_notifier) blocked
   formatters render the event `reason`, clipped to 160 chars.
2. They render event prose because each path built its own text; none
   read the card's stored human_request.
3. The earlier exact-ask fix covered card creation/closeout, not these
   three notification entry paths, and nothing tied them to one contract.
4. Not caught: no test asserted the full ask in each entry path; session
   outcome also promoted a bare wait_state=="human" to a user decision
   without validated request evidence.
5. Root: no shared block presenter + cross-path contract test.

Fix:
- hermes_cli/kanban_block_notice.block_notice(): one read-only presenter
  from current card evidence: validated ask -> "actor: user", full action,
  why, scope, exact @task link (board@gateway for remote); missing/invalid
  request or agent-owned kind -> "actor: agent" (never asks the user);
  card no longer blocked -> "Earlier block resolved; current state".
  user_terminal asks state that the link/unblock grants no terminal
  authority (boundary unchanged).
- All three entry paths use it; gateway wake carries the same text.
- hermes_state_outcome: decisions require a validated human_request.

Tests: tests/tui_gateway/test_actionable_block_notices.py (4 cases x 3
paths, JSON-stored request, wake text, deleted card, outcome both ways).

tests/tui_gateway/test_kanban_failure_notice_text.py pinned the old clipped
"blocked: <reason>" suffix (the defect); it now asserts the same intent
(reason verbatim, no failure-classifier text) plus no false user ask.
